<Docs title="Brand system" description="AgentGuard identity, assets, and usage rules.">
  <div class="doc-title"><span class="section-kicker">PROJECT / BRAND</span><h1>One boundary. One identity.</h1><p>AgentGuard uses a teal boundary glyph to show that agent intent is evaluated before execution.</p></div>
  <h2>Selected direction</h2><p>The boundary glyph is the lead identity. The reviewed gate and agent-path alternatives are retained as vector review artifacts, but are not product marks. Use the shipped SVG variants for navigation, favicon, README, and social cards.</p>
  <div class="docs-table"><div><b>Product name</b><span>AgentGuard in user-facing copy.</span></div><div><b>Repository slug</b><span><code>agent-guard</code> only in URLs, package names, and commands.</span></div><div><b>Palette</b><span>Brand teal #218263, deep teal #17664f, soft mint #effcf7, ink #172420.</span></div><div><b>Status</b><span>Teal is allow/primary, amber is warning, and red is deny/error; never rely on color alone.</span></div></div>
  <p>Review the complete <a href="https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard/blob/master/docs/branding.md">brand system and usage rules ↗</a>.</p>
